+*     RBMK local patch 0013.  A fixed FLOW-RELAX w that damps the slowest
+*     channel slows every other one, and 0.25 does not damp a high-flow
+*     channel whose upper half sits at saturation, where a local quality
+*     makes d(rho)/dh steep (a period-3 cycle of 12 % in G, measured).
+*     Start each channel at w and halve it, down to w/32, whenever a pass
+*     fails to reduce the error; the fixed point is unchanged (at
+*     convergence new = start-of-pass whatever the weight).  Only with
+*     FLOW-RELAX < 1; upstream's default never relaxes.
+      IF((FRLX.LT.1.0).AND.(ITERC.GT.1).AND.(ERR.GE.ERRPRV)) THEN
+        WRLX=MAX(0.5*WRLX,FRLX/32.0)
